cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hybrid Computer Use in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Hybrid Computer Use: A Unified Programmatic, Semantic, and Visual Interface for General Agents"
abstract: >-
  Hybrid Computer Use (HCU) is an open-source MCP server, computer-use, that
  lets coding agents such as Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI and Grok Build
  operate Linux, macOS and Windows desktops. It adds two tools next to the
  agent's own shell and file tools: AX reads and acts on the accessibility
  tree through short refs, batches of up to 64 actions with in-call waits and
  post-action diffs, and GUI works with full-desktop screenshots, zoom and
  batched pointer and keyboard input. Before any input, HCU checks the live
  target of every AX action and the live window layout of every GUI
  coordinate. One Go core drives native providers built on AT-SPI2 and X11,
  AXUIElement and ScreenCaptureKit, and UI Automation and Win32.
